  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A solid cylinder length is suspended symmetrically through two massless strings, as shown in the figure. The distance from the initial rest position, the cylinder should be&nbsp;unbinding the strings to achieve a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p>(take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0092_42eb3edc8f01.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 128px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "120",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The portion of the strings between the ceiling and the cylinder are at rest. Hence, the points of&nbsp;the cylinder where the strings leave it are at rest. The cylinder is thus rolling without slipping on the strings.&nbsp;</p><p>Now, from energy conservation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mgh</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;is moment of inertia of cylinder and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;angular velocity.</p><p>Then, we have</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}